{"name":"Fortune","hex":"#9f97a3","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Fortune","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A surname.","A town in Newfoundland, Newfoundland and Labrador, Canada."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Fortune"}],"entries":[{"title":"Fortuna","blocks":[{"text":"Fortuna, sometimes anglicized as Fortune, is the goddess of luck or fortune in Roman religion. She came to represent life's capriciousness, and was a goddess of fate. In antiquity she was also known by the epithet Automatia. Her Greek equivalent is Tyche."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/97/Fortuna%2C_inv._2244_-_Braccio_Nuovo%2C_Museo_Chiaramonti_-_Vatican_Museums_-_DSC00920.jpg/330px-Fortuna%2C_inv._2244_-_Braccio_Nuovo%2C_Museo_Chiaramonti_-_Vatican_Museums_-_DSC00920.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fortuna","wikidata":"Q4654"},{"title":"Luck","blocks":[{"text":"Luck is a phenomenon or belief that humans may associate with experiencing improbable events, especially improbably positive or negative events.\nPhilosophical naturalism, eschewing any supernatural explanations, might suggest that positive or negative events may happen at any time, and that even improbable events can happen by random chance.\nIn this view, the epithet \"lucky\" or \"unlucky\" is a descriptive label that refers to an event's positivity, negativity, or improbability."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/25/Four-leaf_clover.jpg/330px-Four-leaf_clover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Luck","wikidata":"Q1970348"},{"title":"Fortune (magazine)","blocks":[{"text":"Fortune is an American global business magazine headquartered in New York City. It is published by Fortune Media Group Holdings, a global business media company. The publication was founded by Henry Luce in 1929. The magazine competes with Forbes and Bloomberg Businessweek in the national business magazine category and distinguishes itself with long, in-depth feature articles."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/94/Fortune_magazine_%E2%80%93_June%E2%80%93July_2020_issue.jpg/330px-Fortune_magazine_%E2%80%93_June%E2%80%93July_2020_issue.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fortune_(magazine)","wikidata":"Q372989"},{"title":"Fortune (Chris Brown album)","blocks":[{"text":"Fortune is the fifth studio album by American singer Chris Brown. It was released in the UK on July 2, 2012, and in the US on July 3, 2012, through RCA Records. Production was handled by Brown himself and several record producers, including the Underdogs, Polow da Don, Brian Kennedy, the Runners, the Messengers, H-Money, Danja, and Benny Benassi. The album also features several guest appearances, including Big Sean, Wiz Khalifa, Nas, Sevyn Streeter, and Kevin McCall."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/a/ae/ChrisBrownFortuneAlbumCover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fortune_(Chris_Brown_album)","wikidata":"Q1439131"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/43/CarminaBurana_wheel.jpg/500px-CarminaBurana_wheel.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/43/CarminaBurana_wheel.jpg/1280px-CarminaBurana_wheel.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/43/CarminaBurana_wheel.jpg/500px-CarminaBurana_wheel.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Fortuna governs the circle of the four stages of life, the Wheel of Fortune, in a manuscript 